WEBVTT

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:46.121
Come on, let's say good
night to your brother.

00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:55.153
'Night Sam. Good night, love.

00:00:56.769 --> 00:00:58.154
Hey! Dean.

00:00:58.194 --> 00:01:00.503
Daddy! Hey! Buddy.

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:03.336
What do you think? Sam is ready
to touch around football yet?

00:01:03.336 --> 00:01:05.200
No, daddy. No?

00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:06.931
You got him? I got him.

00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:11.126
Sweet dreams, Sammy.

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:43.482
John?

00:02:04.378 --> 00:02:07.176
John, is he hungry?

00:02:09.314 --> 00:02:10.134
Okay.

00:02:51.719 --> 00:02:53.506
Sammy!

00:03:01.017 --> 00:03:01.734
Mary!

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.702
Mary!

00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:09.245
Mary!

00:03:16.969 --> 00:03:18.214
Hey, Sammy.

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:21.061
Okay?

00:03:38.595 --> 00:03:39.459
Mary!

00:03:53.235 --> 00:03:54.129
Daddy!

00:03:54.222 --> 00:03:55.886
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:03:55.987 --> 00:03:57.300
Don't look back!

00:03:57.486 --> 00:03:58.702
Now, Dean! Go!

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:15.518
It's okay, Sam.

00:04:26.786 --> 00:04:28.834
I got it. I got it.

00:04:32.791 --> 00:04:33.436
Here.

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.576
Stay back. You have to stay back.

00:05:11.456 --> 00:05:11.886
Sam!

00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:14.155
Get a move on, would ya?

00:05:14.156 --> 00:05:16.261
We were supposed to be
there like 15 minutes ago.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:19.041
Sam, you coming or what?

00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:23.322
Do I have to? Yes. It'll be fun.

00:05:24.306 --> 00:05:26.051
And where's your costume?

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.059
You know how I feel about Halloween.

00:05:37.515 --> 00:05:40.376
So here's to Sam and his
awesome LSAT* victory.

00:05:40.483 --> 00:05:41.956
All right, all right.
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:41.957 --> 00:05:44.568
Yeah, he acts all humble,
but he scored a 174.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:48.073
Is that good? Scary good.

00:05:48.115 --> 00:05:50.441
See, there you go. You are
a first-Round draft pick.

00:05:50.956 --> 00:05:52.812
You can go to any law school you want.

00:05:52.813 --> 00:05:55.082
Actually, I got an
interview here monday.

00:05:55.551 --> 00:05:58.706
If it goes okay, I think I got
a shot at a full ride next year.

00:05:58.747 --> 00:06:00.636
Hey, it's gonna go great.

00:06:02.048 --> 00:06:02.773
It better.

00:06:02.805 --> 00:06:05.216
How does it feel to be the
golden boy in your family?

00:06:05.222 --> 00:06:06.281
They don't know.

00:06:06.314 --> 00:06:09.111
No? I would be gloating. Why not?

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:11.185
'Cause we're not exactly the Bradys

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.588
I'm not exactly the
Huxtables. More shots?

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.381
No. No. No. No!

00:06:15.411 --> 00:06:19.460
Seriously, I'm proud of you, and
you're gonna knock them dead on monday.

00:06:19.461 --> 00:06:20.882
You're gonna get that full ride.

00:06:21.245 --> 00:06:22.249
I know it.

00:06:23.086 --> 00:06:24.472
What would I do without you?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.968
Crash and burn.

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.957
Whoa! Easy, tiger.

00:07:30.578 --> 00:07:31.383
Dean?

00:07:33.008 --> 00:07:34.471
You scared the crap out of me.

00:07:34.471 --> 00:07:35.921
That's cause you're out of practice.

00:07:38.293 --> 00:07:39.289
Or not.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:40.941
Get off of me.

00:07:41.206 --> 00:07:42.975
Dean, what the hell are you doing here?

00:07:43.007 --> 00:07:45.182
I was looking for a beer.

00:07:45.699 --> 00:07:47.536
What the hell are you doing here?

00:07:47.636 --> 00:07:49.341
Ok, all right, we got to talk.

00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:52.900
The phone? If I'd called
would you picked up?

00:07:53.426 --> 00:07:54.263
Sam?

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:57.667
Jess, hey.

00:07:58.994 --> 00:08:01.002
Dean, this is my girlfriend, Jessica.

00:08:01.726 --> 00:08:03.567
Wait. Your brother Dean?

00:08:03.686 --> 00:08:04.858
I love the Smurfs.

00:08:05.428 --> 00:08:09.173
You know, I got to tell you. You are
completely out of my brother's league.

00:08:09.279 --> 00:08:10.732
Just let me put something on.

00:08:10.779 --> 00:08:14.587
No, no. No, I wouldn't
dream of it, seriously.

00:08:15.623 --> 00:08:18.746
Anyway, I got to borrow your boyfriend here,
talk about some private family business, but

00:08:18.747 --> 00:08:19.938
Nice meeting you.

00:08:21.571 --> 00:08:22.549
No.

00:08:24.485 --> 00:08:26.586
No, whatever you want to say,
you can say it in front of her.

00:08:27.187 --> 00:08:28.190
Okay.

00:08:29.738 --> 00:08:31.723
Dad hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:32.692 --> 00:08:36.986
So? He's working overtime on a "Miller Time"
shift. He'll stumble back in sooner or later.

00:08:38.002 --> 00:08:40.520
Dad's on a hunting trip,

00:08:40.521 --> 00:08:42.942
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:47.874 --> 00:08:49.034
Jess, excuse us.

00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:52.642
We have to go outside.

00:08:52.868 --> 00:08:57.555
I mean, come on, you can't just break in the middle
of the night and expect me to hit the road with you.

00:08:57.556 --> 00:08:59.641
You're not hearing me,
Sammy. Dad's missing.

00:08:59.656 --> 00:09:01.465
I need you to help me find him.

00:09:01.253 --> 00:09:04.584
You remember the poltergeist in
Amherst, or the devil's gates in Clifton?

00:09:04.656 --> 00:09:07.997
He was missing then, too. He's
always missing, and he's always fine.

00:09:07.998 --> 00:09:10.359
Not for this long. Now, are
you gonna come with me or not?

00:09:10.676 --> 00:09:11.649
I'm not.

00:09:12.039 --> 00:09:12.756
Why not?

00:09:12.804 --> 00:09:15.106
I swore I was done hunting. For good.

00:09:15.361 --> 00:09:18.118
Come on, it wasn't easy,
but it wasn't that bad. Yeah?

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.935
When I told dad I was scared of the
thing in my closet, he gave me a .45.

00:09:21.967 --> 00:09:23.067
What was he supposed to do?

00:09:23.101 --> 00:09:25.030
I was 9 years old.

00:09:25.759 --> 00:09:28.030
He was supposed to say:
"Don't be afraid of the dark."

00:09:28.088 --> 00:09:29.678
"Don't be afraid of the
dark"? Are you kidding me?

00:09:29.679 --> 00:09:31.836
Of course, you should be afraid.
You know what's out there.

00:09:31.877 --> 00:09:34.533
Yeah I know but still... The way
we grew up after mom was killed

00:09:34.546 --> 00:09:37.096
And dad's obsession to find
the thing that killed her.

00:09:37.141 --> 00:09:39.579
But we still haven't
found the damn thing.

00:09:39.709 --> 00:09:41.255
So we kill everything we can find.

00:09:41.387 --> 00:09:43.689
Save a lot of people doing it, too.

00:09:46.273 --> 00:09:48.026
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:09:50.025 --> 00:09:53.779
The weapon training and
melting the silver into bullets?

00:09:53.856 --> 00:09:56.408
Man, Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:09:56.434 --> 00:09:57.475
So, what are you gonna do?

00:09:57.675 --> 00:10:00.419
Are you just gonna live
some normal, apple-Pie life?

00:10:00.036 --> 00:10:01.031
Is that it?

00:10:01.168 --> 00:10:03.487
No, not normal. Safe.

00:10:04.015 --> 00:10:05.772
And that's why you ran away.

00:10:09.182 --> 00:10:10.683
I was just going to college.

00:10:10.684 --> 00:10:13.969
It was dad who said if I was
gonna go, I should stay gone.

00:10:15.492 --> 00:10:16.551
And that's what I'm doing.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:20.513
Dad's in real trouble right now if
he's not dead already. I can feel it.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.846
I can't do this alone.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.465
Yes, you can.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.591
Yeah. Well, I don't want to.

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:39.440
What was he hunting?

00:10:45.343 --> 00:10:48.548
All right. Let's see. Where
the hell did I put that thing?

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:50.590
So when dad left, why
didn't you go with him?

00:10:50.823 --> 00:10:54.353
I was working my own gig... This
voodoo thing down in New Orleans.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.383
Dad let you go on a
hunting trip by yourself?

00:10:57.935 --> 00:10:59.210
I'm 26, dude.

00:11:00.621 --> 00:11:02.350
All right, here we go.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:06.888
So dad was checking out this two-Lane
blacktop just outside of Jericho, California.

00:11:06.987 --> 00:11:08.391
About a month ago, this guy...

00:11:08.656 --> 00:11:11.801
They found his car, but he'd
vanished. Completely M.I.A.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.192
So maybe he was kidnapped.

00:11:14.231 --> 00:11:16.249
Yeah, well, here's another one in April,

00:11:16.393 --> 00:11:21.861
Another one in December '04, '03, '98,
'92... 10 of them over the past 20 years...

00:11:22.156 --> 00:11:24.934
All men, all same
5-Mile stretch of road.

00:11:27.016 --> 00:11:29.103
Started happening more and more, so

00:11:29.136 --> 00:11:30.634
Dad went to go dig around.

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.410
That was about three weeks ago.

00:11:32.815 --> 00:11:35.206
I hadn't heard from him
since, which is bad enough,

00:11:36.446 --> 00:11:38.524
And then I get this
voice mail yesterday.

00:11:39.067 --> 00:11:43.103
<i>Dean, something is starting to
happen. I think it's serious.</i>

00:11:43.191 --> 00:11:45.128
<i>I need to try to figure
out what's going on.</i>

00:11:48.817 --> 00:11:52.078
<i>Be very careful, Dean.
We're all in danger.</i>

00:11:52.746 --> 00:11:54.279
You know there's EVP on that?

00:11:54.377 --> 00:11:57.207
Not bad, Sammy. Kind of
like riding a bike, isn't it?

00:11:57.947 --> 00:12:01.010
All right. I slowed the message
down and ran it through a goldwave,

00:12:01.041 --> 00:12:02.778
Took out the hiss,
and this is what I got.

00:12:04.354 --> 00:12:07.919
<i>I can never go home.</i>

00:12:10.269 --> 00:12:11.865
Never go home.

00:12:17.642 --> 00:12:21.538
You know, in almost two years, I've never
bothered you, never asked you for a thing.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.221
All right, I'll go.

00:12:32.129 --> 00:12:33.615
I'll help you find him,

00:12:33.839 --> 00:12:35.748
But I have to get back
first thing Monday.

00:12:36.108 --> 00:12:37.078
Just wait here.

00:12:37.396 --> 00:12:39.132
What's first thing monday?

00:12:40.607 --> 00:12:42.234
I've this...

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:44.742
I have an interview.

00:12:44.758 --> 00:12:46.567
What? A job interview? Skip it.

00:12:48.374 --> 00:12:52.667
It's a law-School interview, and
it's my whole future on a plate.

00:12:52.739 --> 00:12:53.663
Law school?

00:12:54.543 --> 00:12:56.201
So we got a deal or not?

00:13:00.461 --> 00:13:01.979
Wait, you're taking off?

00:13:02.259 --> 00:13:03.730
Is this about your dad? Is he all right?

00:13:03.871 --> 00:13:06.296
Yeah. You know, just
a little family drama.

00:13:06.769 --> 00:13:09.410
But your brother said he was
on some kind of hunting trip.

00:13:09.465 --> 00:13:12.104
Yeah, he's just deer
hunting up at the cabin,

00:13:12.256 --> 00:13:15.503
And he's probably got Jim,
Jack, and Jose along with him.

00:13:15.506 --> 00:13:17.165
We're just gonna go bring him back.

00:13:17.162 --> 00:13:18.257
What about the interview?

00:13:19.048 --> 00:13:20.206
I'll make the interview.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.750
This is only for a couple days.

00:13:21.856 --> 00:13:24.572
Sam, I mean, please.
Just stop for a second.

00:13:25.514 --> 00:13:26.594
You're sure you're okay?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.570
I'm fine

00:13:29.356 --> 00:13:32.689
It's just... You want
even talk about your family

00:13:33.142 --> 00:13:36.148
And now you're taking off the middle of
the night to spend the week-End with them

00:13:36.367 --> 00:13:39.214
And with Monday coming up...
It's just not kind of your style.

00:13:39.259 --> 00:13:41.570
Hey, everything's gonna be okay.

00:13:42.375 --> 00:13:44.508
I would be back in time, I promise.

00:13:48.224 --> 00:13:49.747
At least tell me where you're going!

00:13:59.819 --> 00:14:01.571
Amy, I can't come over tonight.

00:14:02.543 --> 00:14:05.156
Because I got work in
the morning, that's why.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.020
Okay, I miss it, my
dad's gonna have my ass.

00:14:14.634 --> 00:14:16.370
Hey, uh, Amy, let me call you back.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.181
Car trouble or something?

00:14:36.365 --> 00:14:38.399
Take me home.

00:14:39.917 --> 00:14:41.168
Sure, get in.

00:14:57.389 --> 00:14:59.861
So where do you live?

00:15:02.834 --> 00:15:05.400
At the end of Breckenridge Road.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:09.817
You're coming from a
Halloween party or something?

00:15:13.576 --> 00:15:17.503
You know, um, a girl like you
really shouldn't be alone out here.

00:15:28.813 --> 00:15:30.550
I'm with you.

00:15:42.068 --> 00:15:44.133
Do you think I'm pretty?

00:15:48.936 --> 00:15:50.704
Will you come home with me?

00:15:50.986 --> 00:15:53.770
Um...Hell, yeah.

00:16:13.487 --> 00:16:15.771
Come on. You don't live here.

00:16:17.272 --> 00:16:18.726
I can never go home

00:16:19.086 --> 00:16:23.138
What? What are you talking
about? Nobody lives here.

00:16:23.502 --> 00:16:25.239
Huh, where do you live?

00:16:32.331 --> 00:16:33.974
That's good.

00:16:34.835 --> 00:16:36.290
Joke's over, okay?

00:16:39.652 --> 00:16:41.201
You want me to leave?

00:17:01.028 --> 00:17:01.982
Hello?

00:17:09.421 --> 00:17:10.891
Hello?

00:18:11.627 --> 00:18:13.833
Hey. You want breakfast?

00:18:14.323 --> 00:18:15.434
No, thanks.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:20.315
So how'd you pay for that stuff? You
and dad still running credit-Card scams?

00:18:20.476 --> 00:18:23.762
Yeah, well, hunting ain't
exactly a pro-Ball career.

00:18:25.326 --> 00:18:27.896
Besides, all we do is apply. It's
not our fault they send us the cards.

00:18:27.927 --> 00:18:32.216
Yeah, and what names did you
write on the application this time?

00:18:32.284 --> 00:18:37.935
Uh... Bert Aframian and his son,
Hector. Scored two cards out of the deal.

00:18:38.029 --> 00:18:39.523
Sounds about right.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.643
I swear, man,you got to update
your cassette-Tape collection.

00:18:42.715 --> 00:18:43.435
Why?

00:18:43.576 --> 00:18:45.539
Well, for one... They're cassette tapes.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.540
And two...

00:18:46.541 --> 00:18:50.728
Black Sabbath, Motorhead, Metallica?

00:18:51.095 --> 00:18:53.787
It's the greatest hits of mullet rock.

00:18:54.027 --> 00:18:56.321
House rules, Sammy...
driver picks the music,

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:57.972
Shotgun shuts his cake hole.

00:18:58.739 --> 00:19:01.368
Yo Sammy is a chubby
12-Year-Old. It's...

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:05.154
Sorry, I can't hear you.
The music's too loud.

00:19:21.789 --> 00:19:23.001
Thank you.

00:19:24.211 --> 00:19:27.107
All right. So there's no one matching
dad at the hospital or morgue.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.399
So that's something, I guess.

00:19:31.757 --> 00:19:32.789
Check it out.

00:19:56.488 --> 00:19:57.458
Let's go.

00:20:01.519 --> 00:20:03.272
Did you guys find anything?

00:20:03.303 --> 00:20:05.978
No! Nothing!

00:20:10.865 --> 00:20:14.062
No sign of struggle, no
footprints, no fingerprints...

00:20:14.063 --> 00:20:15.063
Spotless. It's almost too clean.

00:20:15.939 --> 00:20:17.564
So this kid, Troy...

00:20:17.565 --> 00:20:19.563
He's dating your daughter, isn't he? Ya.

00:20:19.564 --> 00:20:20.647
How's Amy doing?

00:20:20.757 --> 00:20:22.806
She's been putting up
missing posters downtown.

00:20:23.901 --> 00:20:26.639
You had another one like
this last month, didn't you?

00:20:27.828 --> 00:20:29.001
And who are you?

00:20:29.549 --> 00:20:30.988
Federal marshals.

00:20:32.526 --> 00:20:34.654
You two are a little young
for marshals, aren't you?

00:20:34.842 --> 00:20:36.500
Thanks, that's awfully kind of you.

00:20:37.068 --> 00:20:38.993
You did have another one
just like this, correct?

00:20:39.149 --> 00:20:39.900
Yeah, that's right,

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.419
About a mile up the road. There
have been others before that.

00:20:42.471 --> 00:20:45.178
So this victim... You knew him?

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:47.931
A town like this,
everybody knows everybody.

00:20:47.994 --> 00:20:50.779
Any connection between the victims
besides that they're all men?

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:52.748
No. Not so far as we can tell.

00:20:53.108 --> 00:20:54.156
So what's the theory?

00:20:54.286 --> 00:20:55.609
Honestly, we don't know...

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:58.031
Serial murderer, kidnapping ring.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:02.140
Well, that is exactly the kind of crack
police work I'd expect out of you guys.

00:21:02.598 --> 00:21:04.585
Thank you for your time.

00:21:05.054 --> 00:21:06.822
Gentlemen.

00:21:15.313 --> 00:21:16.328
What was that for?

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:18.955
Why do you have to step on my foot? Why
do you have to talk to police like that?

00:21:19.165 --> 00:21:21.574
Come on. They don't really
know what's going on.

00:21:21.682 --> 00:21:22.842
We're all alone on this.

00:21:22.843 --> 00:21:25.931
If we're gonna find dad, we've got to
get to the bottom of this thing ourselves.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:29.996
Can I help you boys?

00:21:30.508 --> 00:21:32.308
No, sir. We were just leaving.

00:21:32.309 --> 00:21:34.604
Agent Mulder, agent Scully.

00:21:42.994 --> 00:21:44.324
I'll bet you that's her.

00:21:44.622 --> 00:21:45.529
Yeah.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.221
You must be Amy. Yeah.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:52.574
Troy told us about you. We're his
uncles. I'm Dean. This is Sammy.

00:21:52.809 --> 00:21:54.170
He never mentioned you to me.

00:21:54.749 --> 00:21:55.969
Well, that's Troy, I guess.

00:21:56.016 --> 00:21:57.719
We're not around much.
We're up in Modesto.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:01.630
So we're looking for him, too,
and we're kind of asking around.

00:22:01.835 --> 00:22:04.025
Hey, are you okay? Yeah.

00:22:04.265 --> 00:22:06.471
Do you mind if we ask
you a couple questions?

00:22:07.524 --> 00:22:10.210
I was on the phone with
Troy. He was driving home.

00:22:10.211 --> 00:22:15.064
He said he would call me
right back, and he never did.

00:22:15.065 --> 00:22:17.620
He didn't say anything
strange? Or out of the ordinary?

00:22:17.766 --> 00:22:20.613
No, nothing I can remember.

00:22:22.057 --> 00:22:23.403
I like your necklace.

00:22:26.145 --> 00:22:27.381
Troy gave it to me.

00:22:28.028 --> 00:22:31.955
Mostly to scare my parents...
You know, the devil stuff.

00:22:34.431 --> 00:22:36.650
Actually it means just the opposite.

00:22:36.661 --> 00:22:39.398
A pentagram is a
protection against evil.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:42.504
Really powerfull, I mean if
you believe in a kind of thing.

00:22:42.649 --> 00:22:44.996
Ok, thank you, Unsolved Mysteries.

00:22:45.246 --> 00:22:46.450
Here's the deal, ladies...

00:22:46.451 --> 00:22:49.954
The way Troy disappeared...
Something's not right.

00:22:49.955 --> 00:22:52.058
So if you've heard anything...

00:22:54.351 --> 00:22:55.259
What is it?

00:22:55.947 --> 00:22:56.877
Well, it's just...

00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:59.906
I mean, with all these guys
going missing, people talk.

00:22:59.952 --> 00:23:01.141
What do they talk about?

00:23:04.916 --> 00:23:07.028
It's kind of this local legend.

00:23:07.294 --> 00:23:11.925
This one girl, she got murdered
out on Centennial like decades ago.

00:23:12.529 --> 00:23:15.173
Well, supposedly, she's still out there.

00:23:15.569 --> 00:23:18.959
She hitchhikes, and
whoever picks her up...

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:22.132
Well, they disappear forever.

00:23:39.232 --> 00:23:41.062
Let me try. I got it.

00:23:42.423 --> 00:23:43.268
Dude.

00:23:44.785 --> 00:23:46.944
You're such a control freak.

00:23:47.679 --> 00:23:50.667
So angry spirits are born out
of violent death, right? Yeah

00:23:51.043 --> 00:23:52.451
Maybe it's not murder.

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:06.673
This was 1981. Constance Welch, 24 years old,
jumps off Sylvania Bridge, drowns in the river.

00:24:06.704 --> 00:24:08.461
Does it say why she did it? Yeah.

00:24:08.852 --> 00:24:09.415
What?

00:24:10.151 --> 00:24:12.502
An hour before they
found her, she calls 911.

00:24:12.565 --> 00:24:15.716
Her two little kids are in the bathtub.
She leaves them alone for a minute,

00:24:15.717 --> 00:24:16.889
And when she comes back,

00:24:16.961 --> 00:24:18.213
They aren't breathing.

00:24:18.893 --> 00:24:19.910
Both died.

00:24:20.901 --> 00:24:23.488
"Our babies were gone, and
Constance just couldn't bear it,"

00:24:23.489 --> 00:24:24.489
Said husband, Joseph Welch.

00:24:26.867 --> 00:24:28.964
That bridge look familiar to you?

00:24:33.959 --> 00:24:36.963
So this is where Constance
took the swan dive.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:39.111
So you think dad would have been here?

00:24:39.893 --> 00:24:42.615
Well, he's chasing the same
story, and we're chasing him.

00:24:44.028 --> 00:24:45.374
Okay, so now what?

00:24:46.359 --> 00:24:48.909
Now we keep digging till we
find him. It might take a while.

00:24:49.107 --> 00:24:52.721
Dean, I told you I've got
to get back by... Monday.

00:24:53.863 --> 00:24:55.631
Right. The interview.

00:24:55.678 --> 00:24:57.258
Yeah. Yeah, I forgot.

00:24:57.921 --> 00:24:59.767
You're really serious
about this, aren't you?

00:25:00.768 --> 00:25:02.974
You think you're just
gonna become some lawyer,

00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:04.601
Marry your girl?

00:25:04.664 --> 00:25:05.806
Maybe. Why not?

00:25:06.014 --> 00:25:09.394
Does Jessica know the truth about you?
Does she know about the things you've done?

00:25:09.597 --> 00:25:11.365
No, and she's not ever going to know.

00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:13.602
Well, that's healthy.

00:25:13.904 --> 00:25:18.425
You can pretend all you want, Sammy, but sooner or
later you're gonna have to face up to who you really are.

00:25:18.852 --> 00:25:19.611
Who is that?

00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:21.117
One of us. No!

00:25:21.246 --> 00:25:23.787
I'm not like you. This is
not going to be my life.

00:25:23.810 --> 00:25:26.878
Well, you have a responsibility. To dad?

00:25:26.206 --> 00:25:27.911
And his crusade?

00:25:28.286 --> 00:25:31.337
If it weren't for pictures, I
wouldn't even know what mom looks like.

00:25:31.732 --> 00:25:33.109
What difference would it make?

00:25:33.359 --> 00:25:35.503
Even if we do find the
thing that killed her,

00:25:36.301 --> 00:25:39.086
Mom's gone, and she isn't coming back.

00:25:45.329 --> 00:25:47.675
Don't talk about her like that.

00:25:56.872 --> 00:25:57.795
Sam.

00:26:10.621 --> 00:26:12.420
Where'd she go? I don't know.

00:26:16.779 --> 00:26:20.424
What the...? Who's driving your car?

00:26:28.108 --> 00:26:30.955
Come on, Dean. Let's go! Go!

00:26:57.356 --> 00:26:58.216
Dean!

00:26:59.637 --> 00:27:00.310
Dean!

00:27:03.134 --> 00:27:03.979
What?!

00:27:07.745 --> 00:27:09.920
Hey, are you all right?

00:27:10.859 --> 00:27:12.032
I'm super.

00:27:17.740 --> 00:27:19.054
Car all right?

00:27:19.257 --> 00:27:21.854
Yeah, whatever she did to
it, it seems all right now.

00:27:22.089 --> 00:27:24.233
That Constance chick... What a bitch!

00:27:24.467 --> 00:27:27.236
Well, she doesn't want us
digging around, that's for sure.

00:27:29.197 --> 00:27:31.481
So where's the trail
go from here, genius?

00:27:36.973 --> 00:27:38.553
You smell like a toilet.

00:27:41.565 --> 00:27:42.785
One room, please.

00:27:46.649 --> 00:27:48.543
You guys having a reunion or something?

00:27:48.840 --> 00:27:49.513
What do you mean?

00:27:49.846 --> 00:27:54.273
That other guy, Bert Aframian. He came in
and bought out a room for the whole month.

00:28:24.939 --> 00:28:27.500
I don't think he's been here
for a couple days at least.

00:28:29.664 --> 00:28:32.323
Salt, cat's-Eye shells...

00:28:32.746 --> 00:28:36.506
He was worried, trying to
keep something from coming in.

00:28:39.525 --> 00:28:40.636
What do you got here?

00:28:41.104 --> 00:28:43.717
Centennial Highway victims.

00:28:45.266 --> 00:28:46.596
I don't get it.

00:28:47.159 --> 00:28:51.070
I mean, different men,
different jobs, age, ethnicities.

00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:53.548
There's always a connection, right?

00:28:54.377 --> 00:28:55.801
What do these guys have in common?

00:29:10.930 --> 00:29:12.260
Dad figured it out.

00:29:12.529 --> 00:29:13.781
What do you mean?

00:29:13.829 --> 00:29:15.898
He found the same article we did.

00:29:15.899 --> 00:29:19.313
Constance Welch. She's a woman in white.

00:29:22.288 --> 00:29:23.774
You sly dogs.

00:29:24.071 --> 00:29:27.435
All right, so if we're dealing with a woman in white,
dad would have found the corpse and destroyed it.

00:29:27.623 --> 00:29:29.219
She might have another weakness.

00:29:29.743 --> 00:29:32.270
No, dad would want to
make sure. He'd dig her up.

00:29:32.329 --> 00:29:33.693
Does it say where she's buried?

00:29:34.117 --> 00:29:35.916
No, not that I can tell.

00:29:36.433 --> 00:29:38.639
If I were dad, though,
I'd go ask her husband,

00:29:39.061 --> 00:29:40.313
If he's still alive.

00:29:46.882 --> 00:29:50.027
All right, why don't you see if you can
find an address? I'm gonna get cleaned up.

00:29:50.469 --> 00:29:55.366
Hey, Dean, what I said earlier
about mom and dad... I'm sorry.

00:29:56.195 --> 00:29:57.618
No chick-Flick moments.

00:29:58.797 --> 00:30:00.596
All right... jerk.

00:30:01.738 --> 00:30:02.614
Bitch.

00:30:19.936 --> 00:30:23.362
<i>Hey, it's me. It's about 10:20...</i>

00:30:23.878 --> 00:30:28.077
Hey, man. I'm starving. I'm gonna grab a little
something to eat at that diner down the street.

00:30:28.078 --> 00:30:29.386
You want anything?

00:30:29.693 --> 00:30:30.262
No.

00:30:30.262 --> 00:30:31.559
Aframian's buying.

00:30:49.055 --> 00:30:51.590
<i>So come home soon, okay? I love you.</i>

00:30:54.453 --> 00:30:54.985
What?

00:30:55.224 --> 00:30:56.554
Dude, five-O. Take off.

00:30:57.023 --> 00:30:58.040
What about you?

00:30:58.306 --> 00:31:00.903
Uh, they kind of
spotted me. Go find dad.

00:31:02.875 --> 00:31:04.064
Problem, officers?

00:31:04.236 --> 00:31:05.487
Where's your partner?

00:31:05.736 --> 00:31:07.786
Partner? What? What partner?

00:31:15.227 --> 00:31:18.825
So fake U.S. Marshal, fake credit cards.

00:31:19.091 --> 00:31:20.546
You got anything that's real?

00:31:21.094 --> 00:31:22.001
My boobs.

00:31:23.933 --> 00:31:26.076
You have the right to remain silent.

00:31:28.382 --> 00:31:30.572
So you want to give us your real name?

00:31:30.922 --> 00:31:34.176
I told you. It's Nugent, Ted Nugent.

00:31:36.366 --> 00:31:39.370
I'm not sure you realize just
how much trouble you're in here.

00:31:39.371 --> 00:31:43.724
We're talking, like, misdemeanor kind of
trouble or "squeal like a pig" trouble?

00:31:44.084 --> 00:31:46.838
You got the faces of 10 missing
persons taped to your wall,

00:31:47.250 --> 00:31:50.160
Along with a whole lot
of satanic mumbo jumbo.

00:31:50.535 --> 00:31:52.475
Boy, you are officially a suspect.

00:31:52.637 --> 00:31:56.611
That makes sense 'cause when the
first one went missing in '82, I was 3.

00:31:57.158 --> 00:32:00.068
I know you got partners.
One of them's an older guy.

00:32:00.851 --> 00:32:02.822
Maybe he started the whole thing.

00:32:04.501 --> 00:32:06.707
So tell me, Dean...

00:32:09.106 --> 00:32:10.029
Is this his?

00:32:17.606 --> 00:32:19.108
I thought that might be your name.

00:32:20.735 --> 00:32:22.281
See, I leafed through this,

00:32:22.295 --> 00:32:25.872
What little I could make out. I
mean, it's nine kinds of crazy,

00:32:27.472 --> 00:32:29.193
But I found this, too.

00:32:30.269 --> 00:32:35.964
Now, you're staying right here till you
tell me exactly what the hell that means.

00:32:48.257 --> 00:32:51.386
Hi, uh, are you Joseph Welch? Yeah.

00:32:52.272 --> 00:32:54.013
Yeah, he was older, but that's him.

00:32:54.095 --> 00:32:57.462
He came by three or four days
ago, said he was a reporter.

00:32:57.821 --> 00:33:00.293
That's right. We're
working on a story together.

00:33:01.542 --> 00:33:05.563
Well, I don't know what the hell kind of story
you're working on... the questions he asked me.

00:33:05.641 --> 00:33:07.471
About your late wife, Constance.

00:33:08.441 --> 00:33:10.178
He asked me where she was buried.

00:33:11.028 --> 00:33:12.639
And where is that again?

00:33:13.249 --> 00:33:14.767
What? I got to go through these twice?

00:33:15.064 --> 00:33:17.409
It's fact checking, if you don't mind.

00:33:20.037 --> 00:33:23.448
In a plot behind my old
place over on Breckenridge.

00:33:24.063 --> 00:33:25.612
Why did you move?

00:33:27.035 --> 00:33:30.477
I'm not gonna live in the
house where my children died.

00:33:33.193 --> 00:33:35.274
Mr. Welch, did you ever marry again?

00:33:35.399 --> 00:33:39.013
No way. Constance... She
was the love of my life,

00:33:40.607 --> 00:33:42.438
Prettiest woman I ever known.

00:33:42.657 --> 00:33:44.096
So you had a happy marriage?

00:33:47.613 --> 00:33:48.411
Definitely.

00:33:51.493 --> 00:33:54.215
Well, that should do
it. Thanks for your time.

00:34:04.801 --> 00:34:07.639
Mr. Welch, you ever
hear of a woman in white?

00:34:07.821 --> 00:34:08.556
A what?

00:34:09.025 --> 00:34:12.170
A woman in white or
sometimes a weeping woman.

00:34:13.207 --> 00:34:14.193
It's a ghost story.

00:34:14.416 --> 00:34:17.718
Well, it's more of a phenomenon, really.

00:34:18.020 --> 00:34:21.494
They're spirits. They've been
sighted for hundreds of years,

00:34:21.854 --> 00:34:26.068
Dozens of places in Hawaii and
Mexico, lately in Arizona, Indiana.

00:34:26.109 --> 00:34:27.987
All these are different
women, you understand,

00:34:28.273 --> 00:34:30.150
But all share the same story.

00:34:31.089 --> 00:34:34.254
Boy, I don't care much for nonsense.

00:34:34.411 --> 00:34:35.772
You see, when they were alive,

00:34:36.215 --> 00:34:38.249
Their husbands were unfaithful to them,

00:34:39.156 --> 00:34:40.236
And these women,

00:34:40.596 --> 00:34:43.662
Basically suffering from temporary
insanity, murdered their children.

00:34:45.332 --> 00:34:48.680
Then, once they realized what they
had done, they took their own lives.

00:34:48.977 --> 00:34:50.729
So now their spirits are cursed,

00:34:51.058 --> 00:34:53.076
Walking back roads, waterways,

00:34:53.410 --> 00:34:56.476
And if they find an
unfaithful man, they kill him,

00:34:56.914 --> 00:34:58.651
And that man is never seen again.

00:35:00.294 --> 00:35:01.764
You think...

00:35:02.921 --> 00:35:06.614
You think that has something
to do with Constance,

00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:08.413
You smart ass?

00:35:09.007 --> 00:35:10.149
You tell me.

00:35:13.574 --> 00:35:18.048
I mean, maybe... Maybe
I made some mistakes,

00:35:18.627 --> 00:35:20.301
But no matter what I did,

00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:23.728
Constance never would have
killed her own children.

00:35:25.156 --> 00:35:27.253
Now, you get the hell out of here,

00:35:27.691 --> 00:35:29.302
And you don't come back.

00:35:44.779 --> 00:35:46.750
I don't know how many
times I got to tell you.

00:35:46.969 --> 00:35:48.581
It's my high-School locker combo.

00:35:49.008 --> 00:35:50.698
Are we gonna do this all night long?

00:35:50.776 --> 00:35:53.858
We just got a 911. Shots
fired over at Whiteford Road.

00:35:55.814 --> 00:35:57.331
Do you have to go to the bathroom?

00:35:57.962 --> 00:35:58.604
No.

00:35:58.932 --> 00:35:59.996
Good.

00:36:49.987 --> 00:36:53.179
Fake 911 phone call, Sammy?
That's pretty illegal.

00:36:53.460 --> 00:36:54.227
You're welcome.

00:36:54.321 --> 00:36:55.604
Listen, we got to talk

00:36:55.697 --> 00:36:58.440
Tell me about it. So the
husband was unfaithful.

00:36:58.534 --> 00:37:00.223
We are dealing with a woman in white.

00:37:00.301 --> 00:37:02.874
She's buried behind her old house.

00:37:02.895 --> 00:37:04.095
Sammy, would you shut up for a second?

00:37:04.139 --> 00:37:06.267
I can't figure out why he
hasn't destroyed the corpse yet.

00:37:06.470 --> 00:37:08.911
That's what I'm trying
to tell you. He's gone.

00:37:09.307 --> 00:37:10.386
Dad left Jericho.

00:37:10.433 --> 00:37:12.279
What? How do you know?

00:37:13.093 --> 00:37:13.906
I've got his journal.

00:37:14.094 --> 00:37:15.705
He doesn't go anywhere
without that thing.

00:37:15.898 --> 00:37:16.993
Well, he did this time.

00:37:17.056 --> 00:37:17.807
What's it say?

00:37:17.838 --> 00:37:20.936
Same old ex-Marine crap when he
wants to let us know where he's going.

00:37:20.999 --> 00:37:21.807
Coordinates.

00:37:21.810 --> 00:37:22.810
Where to?

00:37:22.810 --> 00:37:23.977
I'm not sure yet.

00:37:24.002 --> 00:37:28.100
I don't understand. I mean,
what can be so important

00:37:28.101 --> 00:37:29.101
That he just gets out
in the middle of the job?

00:37:28.717 --> 00:37:30.484
Dean, what the hell is going on?

00:37:33.956 --> 00:37:35.348
Sam, Sam!

00:37:41.757 --> 00:37:43.165
Take me home.

00:37:51.135 --> 00:37:53.341
Take me home.

00:37:55.176 --> 00:37:55.958
No.

00:38:36.811 --> 00:38:38.062
Don't do this.

00:38:40.649 --> 00:38:42.260
I can never go home.

00:38:45.300 --> 00:38:47.130
You're scared to go home.

00:38:54.144 --> 00:38:55.224
Hold me.

00:38:56.303 --> 00:38:58.760
I'm so cold.

00:38:59.171 --> 00:39:03.160
You can't kill me. I'm not unfaithful.

00:39:03.395 --> 00:39:05.194
I've never been.

00:39:06.409 --> 00:39:07.473
You will be.

00:39:52.088 --> 00:39:53.434
I'm taking you home.

00:39:55.905 --> 00:39:56.468
Sam!

00:40:07.554 --> 00:40:09.322
Sam! Here!

00:40:09.369 --> 00:40:10.511
You okay?

00:40:11.199 --> 00:40:12.075
I think.

00:40:12.670 --> 00:40:14.798
Can you move? Yeah. Help me.

00:41:16.177 --> 00:41:18.351
You've come home to us, mommy.

00:41:56.460 --> 00:41:58.431
So this is where she drowned her kids.

00:42:00.105 --> 00:42:01.576
That's why she could never go home.

00:42:03.367 --> 00:42:05.119
She was too scared to face them.

00:42:06.379 --> 00:42:07.959
You found her weak spot.

00:42:08.428 --> 00:42:09.711
Nice work, Sammy.

00:42:12.297 --> 00:42:14.441
I wish I could say the same for you.

00:42:14.566 --> 00:42:16.859
What were you thinking shooting
Casper in the face, you freak?

00:42:16.964 --> 00:42:19.468
Hey, saved your ass.

00:42:20.359 --> 00:42:23.379
I'll tell you another thing.
If you screwed up my car,

00:42:24.942 --> 00:42:26.162
I'll kill you.

00:42:38.735 --> 00:42:41.973
Okay, here's where dad went. It's
called Blackbottle Ridge, Colorado.

00:42:43.209 --> 00:42:44.977
Sounds charming. How far?

00:42:45.191 --> 00:42:47.052
About 600 miles.

00:42:47.756 --> 00:42:50.087
If we shag ass, we
can make it by morning.

00:42:51.976 --> 00:42:53.540
Dean, um...

00:42:56.122 --> 00:42:57.154
You're not going.

00:42:57.295 --> 00:42:59.720
The interview's in 10
hours. I got to be there.

00:43:04.536 --> 00:43:08.651
Yeah. Yeah, whatever.
I'll take you home.

00:43:29.244 --> 00:43:30.731
You'll call me if you find him?

00:43:33.739 --> 00:43:35.476
Maybe I can meet up with you later, huh?

00:43:35.773 --> 00:43:36.633
Yeah, all right.

00:43:40.635 --> 00:43:41.417
Sam.

00:43:45.485 --> 00:43:47.237
You know, we made a hell
of a team back there.

00:43:48.479 --> 00:43:49.073
Yeah.

00:44:08.328 --> 00:44:09.204
Jess!

00:44:11.082 --> 00:44:12.208
You home!?

00:44:54.347 --> 00:44:55.286
No!

00:44:58.232 --> 00:44:59.202
Sam!

00:44:59.233 --> 00:45:00.000
Jess!

00:45:01.752 --> 00:45:03.270
Sam! Sam!

00:45:04.521 --> 00:45:06.320
No! No!

00:45:07.237 --> 00:45:09.991
Jess! Jess! No!

00:45:55.992 --> 00:45:57.713
We got work to do.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
